config ENCODER_QDEC_STM32
	bool "STM32 timer quadrature encoder driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_FIBRIL_STM32_QDEC_ENABLED
	select PINCTRL
	help
	  Enable support for a quadrature encoder decoded by an STM32 general
	  purpose timer. The timer counts edges in hardware; the driver samples
	  the counter periodically so that the accumulated position stays
	  continuous across the counter's wrap.

	  This is not the upstream st,stm32-qdec driver. That one sets the
	  timer's auto-reload to a multiple of the counts per revolution and
	  does not publish the value, which leaves a consumer unable to tell
	  where the counter wraps.
